IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-medium.l4: Chapter 12, ss 465 to 467 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): companies qualifying as medium-sized
-- (general, and parent companies), and the companies excluded from being treated as medium-sized.
-- Lines 6348-6406 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the rule; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The pounds and the number of employees in the tables are the Act's own figures (they are in the text, not left to
-- regulations), so they are written into the rules. The facts of a company (its turnover and so on) are inputs.
-- This part answers s 465 to 467 for the others (PLAN.md section 4.2): `s 465 the company qualifies as medium-sized`.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 465: companies qualifying as medium-sized: general
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (4): for a financial year that is not in fact a year, "the maximum figures for turnover must be proportionately adjusted".
-- The text does not say by what measure; the length of the year is taken in months (12 for a year), fork F8 in NOTES.md.
-- src:6359 | (4) For a period that is a company's financial year but not in fact a year the maximum figures for turnover must be proportionately adjusted.
@ref s 465(4) The maximum figure for turnover is adjusted proportionately for a financial year that is not a year (src:6359)
GIVEN `the length of the financial year in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 465(4) the maximum figure for turnover for the financial year` MEANS
    54000000 TIMES (`the length of the financial year in months` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- (3): two or more of three requirements.
-- src:6356 | 1. Turnover | Not more than £54 million
@ref s 465(3) Requirement 1: turnover not more than £54 million (src:6356)
GIVEN `the turnover of the company in the financial year (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the financial year in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 465(3) the requirement for turnover is satisfied` MEANS
    `the turnover of the company in the financial year (in pounds)` AT MOST `s 465(4) the maximum figure for turnover for the financial year` `the length of the financial year in months`

-- src:6357 | 2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £27 million
@ref s 465(3) Requirement 2: balance sheet total not more than £27 million (src:6357)
GIVEN `the balance sheet total of the company (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 465(3) the requirement for the balance sheet total is satisfied` MEANS
    `the balance sheet total of the company (in pounds)` AT MOST 27000000

-- src:6358 | 3. Number of employees | Not more than 250
@ref s 465(3) Requirement 3: number of employees not more than 250 (src:6358)
GIVEN `the number of employees of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 465(3) the requirement for the number of employees is satisfied` MEANS
    `the number of employees of the company` AT MOST 250

-- src:6355 | (3) The qualifying conditions are met by a company in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements—
@ref s 465(3) The qualifying conditions are met in a year in which the company satisfies two or more of the requirements (src:6355)
GIVEN `the turnover of the company in the financial year (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the financial year in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the balance sheet total of the company (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of employees of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(3) the qualifying conditions are met` MEANS
    IF (   (IF `s 465(3) the requirement for turnover is satisfied` `the turnover of the company in the financial year (in pounds)` `the length of the financial year in months` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `s 465(3) the requirement for the balance sheet total is satisfied` `the balance sheet total of the company (in pounds)` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `s 465(3) the requirement for the number of employees is satisfied` `the number of employees of the company` THEN 1 ELSE 0)) AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "satisfies two or more" not met): "The qualifying conditions are met by a company in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements"

-- (5): the balance sheet total is the aggregate of the amounts shown as assets in the balance sheet.
-- src:6360 | (5) The balance sheet total means the aggregate of the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet.
@ref s 465(5) The balance sheet total is the aggregate of the amounts shown as assets (src:6360)
GIVEN `the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet (in pounds)` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 465(5) the balance sheet total` MEANS
    sum `the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet (in pounds)`

-- (6): the number of employees is the average over the months of the financial year of the persons employed under contracts of service.
-- src:6361 | (6) The number of employees means the average number of persons employed by the company in the year, determined as follows—
-- src:6362 | (a) find for each month in the financial year the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in that month (whether throughout the month or not),
-- src:6363 | (b) add together the monthly totals, and
-- src:6364 | (c) divide by the number of months in the financial year.
@ref s 465(6) The number of employees is the average of the monthly numbers (src:6361-6364)
GIVEN `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year (whether throughout the month or not)` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 465(6) the number of employees` MEANS
    IF null `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year (whether throughout the month or not)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text divides "by the number of months in the financial year" and a financial year has months
    ELSE JUST ((sum `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year (whether throughout the month or not)`) DIVIDED BY (count `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year (whether throughout the month or not)`))

-- (1): first financial year; (2): a subsequent financial year.
-- src:6350 | (1) A company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to its first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year.
@ref s 465(1) First financial year: medium-sized if the qualifying conditions are met (src:6350)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(1) the company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to its first financial year` MEANS
    IF `the qualifying conditions are met in that year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "A company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to its first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year."

-- src:6351 | (2) A company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year—
-- src:6352 | (a) if the qualifying conditions are met in that year and the preceding financial year;
-- src:6353 | (b) if the qualifying conditions are met in that year and the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year;
-- src:6354 | (c) if the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year and the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to that year.
@ref s 465(2) A subsequent financial year: three ways to qualify (src:6351-6354)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(2) the company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    IF    (`the qualifying conditions are met in that year` AND `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year`)
       OR (`the qualifying conditions are met in that year` AND `the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year`)
       OR (`the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year` AND `the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met in each of (a), (b) and (c)): "A company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year— (a) if the qualifying conditions are met in that year and the preceding financial year; (b) if ... and the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year; (c) if the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year and the company qualified as medium-sized in relation to that year"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 466: companies qualifying as medium-sized: parent companies
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (5): the aggregate figures aggregate the figures determined under s 465 for each member of the group.
-- src:6377 | (5) The aggregate figures are ascertained by aggregating the relevant figures determined in accordance with section 465 for each member of the group.
@ref s 466(5) The aggregate figures (src:6377)
GIVEN `the figures determined in accordance with section 465 for each member of the group` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 466(5) the aggregate figure` MEANS
    sum `the figures determined in accordance with section 465 for each member of the group`

-- (6): "net" and "gross".
-- src:6379 | “net” means after any set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions—
-- src:6380 | (a) in the case of Companies Act accounts, in accordance with regulations under section 404,
-- src:6381 | (b) in the case of IAS accounts, in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards; and
@ref s 466(6) "net": after set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions (src:6379-6381)
GIVEN `the figure is after any set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those set-offs and adjustments follow regulations under section 404 (Companies Act accounts) or UK-adopted international accounting standards (IAS accounts)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(6) the figure is a net figure` MEANS
    IF `the figure is after any set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions` AND `those set-offs and adjustments follow regulations under section 404 (Companies Act accounts) or UK-adopted international accounting standards (IAS accounts)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“net” means after any set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions— (a) in the case of Companies Act accounts, in accordance with regulations under section 404, (b) in the case of IAS accounts, in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards"

-- src:6382 | “gross” means without those set-offs and other adjustments.
@ref s 466(6) "gross": without those set-offs and other adjustments (src:6382)
GIVEN `the figure is without the set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(6) the figure is a gross figure` MEANS
    IF `the figure is without the set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“gross” means without those set-offs and other adjustments"

-- (4): the group requirements, each satisfied on the net or the gross figure.
-- src:6374 | 1. Aggregate turnover | Not more than £54 million net (or £64 million gross)
@ref s 466(4) Requirement 1: aggregate turnover not more than £54 million net (or £64 million gross) (src:6374)
GIVEN `the aggregate turnover, net (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate turnover, gross (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 466(4) the requirement for aggregate turnover is satisfied` MEANS
    `the aggregate turnover, net (in pounds)` AT MOST 54000000 OR `the aggregate turnover, gross (in pounds)` AT MOST 64000000

-- src:6375 | 2. Aggregate balance sheet total | Not more than £27 million net (or £32 million gross)
@ref s 466(4) Requirement 2: aggregate balance sheet total not more than £27 million net (or £32 million gross) (src:6375)
GIVEN `the aggregate balance sheet total, net (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate balance sheet total, gross (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 466(4) the requirement for the aggregate balance sheet total is satisfied` MEANS
    `the aggregate balance sheet total, net (in pounds)` AT MOST 27000000 OR `the aggregate balance sheet total, gross (in pounds)` AT MOST 32000000

-- src:6376 | 3. Aggregate number of employees | Not more than 250
@ref s 466(4) Requirement 3: aggregate number of employees not more than 250 (src:6376)
GIVEN `the aggregate number of employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 466(4) the requirement for the aggregate number of employees is satisfied` MEANS
    `the aggregate number of employees` AT MOST 250

-- src:6373 | (4) The qualifying conditions are met by a group in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements—
-- src:6383 | A company may satisfy any relevant requirement on the basis of either the net or the gross figure.
@ref s 466(4) The group's qualifying conditions are met in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the requirements (src:6373 and src:6383)
GIVEN `the aggregate turnover, net (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate turnover, gross (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate balance sheet total, net (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate balance sheet total, gross (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate number of employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(4) the qualifying conditions are met by the group` MEANS
    IF (   (IF `s 466(4) the requirement for aggregate turnover is satisfied` `the aggregate turnover, net (in pounds)` `the aggregate turnover, gross (in pounds)` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `s 466(4) the requirement for the aggregate balance sheet total is satisfied` `the aggregate balance sheet total, net (in pounds)` `the aggregate balance sheet total, gross (in pounds)` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `s 466(4) the requirement for the aggregate number of employees is satisfied` `the aggregate number of employees` THEN 1 ELSE 0)) AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "satisfies two or more" not met): "The qualifying conditions are met by a group in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements"

-- (7): the figures for each subsidiary undertaking are those in its individual accounts for the relevant financial year: its
-- financial year that ends with the parent's, or, if none does, the one ending last before the end of the parent's.
-- src:6384 | (7) The figures for each subsidiary undertaking shall be those included in its individual accounts for the relevant financial year, that is—
-- src:6385 | (a) if its financial year ends with that of the parent company, that financial year, and
-- src:6386 | (b) if not, its financial year ending last before the end of the financial year of the parent company.
@ref s 466(7) The financial year of a subsidiary undertaking whose figures are used (src:6384-6386)
GIVEN `the end of the parent company's financial year` IS A DATE
      `the ends of the subsidiary undertaking's financial years` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 466(7) the end of the subsidiary undertaking's financial year whose figures are used` MEANS
    LET `those that end on or before the end of the parent company's financial year` MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD d AT MOST `the end of the parent company's financial year`) `the ends of the subsidiary undertaking's financial years`
    IN IF null `those that end on or before the end of the parent company's financial year`
       THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names no year when the subsidiary undertaking has no financial year ending on or before the end of the parent company's
       ELSE JUST (foldl (GIVEN best, d YIELD IF d AT LEAST best THEN d ELSE best) (at `those that end on or before the end of the parent company's financial year` 0) `those that end on or before the end of the parent company's financial year`)

DECLARE `s 466 figures to take` IS ONE OF
    `s 466 the figures included in the subsidiary undertaking's individual accounts for the relevant financial year`
    `s 466 the latest available figures`

-- src:6387 | If those figures cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay, the latest available figures shall be taken.
@ref s 466(7) If the figures cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay, the latest available figures are taken (src:6387)
GIVEN `the figures cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 466 figures to take`
`s 466(7) the figures to take for the subsidiary undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the figures cannot be obtained without disproportionate expense or undue delay`
    THEN `s 466 the latest available figures`
    ELSE `s 466 the figures included in the subsidiary undertaking's individual accounts for the relevant financial year`

-- (1): a parent company qualifies as medium-sized only if the group headed by it qualifies. "only if" is a necessary
-- condition: it says no when the group does not qualify, and does not say yes when it does.
-- src:6367 | (1) A parent company qualifies as a medium-sized company in relation to a financial year only if the group headed by it qualifies as a medium-sized group.
@ref s 466(1) A parent company qualifies as medium-sized only if the group headed by it qualifies (src:6367)
GIVEN `the group headed by the parent company qualifies as a medium-sized group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(1) the parent company qualifies as a medium-sized company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the group headed by the parent company qualifies as a medium-sized group`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "only if"): "A parent company qualifies as a medium-sized company in relation to a financial year only if the group headed by it qualifies as a medium-sized group."
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" states a necessary condition and does not say the parent company qualifies when the group does
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group qualifies is not known

-- (2) and (3): the group qualifies in the parent company's first or a subsequent financial year (the same three limbs as s 465(2)).
-- src:6368 | (2) A group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to the parent company's first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year.
@ref s 466(2) A group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to the parent company's first financial year (src:6368)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(2) the group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to the parent company's first financial year` MEANS
    IF `the qualifying conditions are met in that year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "A group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to the parent company's first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year."

-- src:6369 | (3) A group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year of the parent company—
-- src:6370 | (a) if the qualifying conditions are met in that year and the preceding financial year;
-- src:6371 | (b) if the qualifying conditions are met in that year and the group qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year;
-- src:6372 | (c) if the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year and the group qualified as medium-sized in relation to that year.
@ref s 466(3) A group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year of the parent company (src:6369-6372)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 466(3) the group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    IF    (`the qualifying conditions are met in that year` AND `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year`)
       OR (`the qualifying conditions are met in that year` AND `the group qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year`)
       OR (`the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding financial year` AND `the group qualified as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met in each of (a), (b) and (c)): "A group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year of the parent company— (a) if ...; (b) if ...; (c) if ..."

-- (7) of s 465: the section is subject to s 466. A parent company qualifies under s 465 only if its group qualifies (s 466(1)):
-- the group's answer (from s 466(2), (3) and (4)) defeats the company's when it is no, and leaves it standing when it is yes.
-- src:6365 | (7) This section is subject to section 466 (companies qualifying as medium-sized: parent companies).
@ref s 465(7) This section is subject to section 466 (src:6365)
GIVEN `the section 465 answer for the company (subsection (1) or (2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the group headed by the parent company qualifies as a medium-sized group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 465(7) the company qualifies as medium-sized, subject to section 466` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section 465 answer for the company (subsection (1) or (2))`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 465(1) and (2) answer no
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the section 465 answer is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a parent company is not known
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            CONSIDER `the group headed by the parent company qualifies as a medium-sized group`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "only if"): "A parent company qualifies as a medium-sized company in relation to a financial year only if the group headed by it qualifies as a medium-sized group."
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- the "only if" of section 466(1) is met, so section 465's answer stands
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group qualifies is not known

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 467: companies excluded from being treated as medium-sized
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (3): a company is a small company for subsection (2) if it qualified as small in relation to its last financial year
-- ending on or before the end of the financial year in question. The small-company answer is s 382's (coa8), an INPUT.
-- src:6405 | (3) A company is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2) if it qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year in question.
@ref s 467(3) A small company for the purposes of subsection (2) (src:6405)
GIVEN `s 382 the company qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year in question` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(3) the company is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    `s 382 the company qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year in question`

-- (2): each member of the group, with the facts the paragraphs name.
-- src:6397 | (2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is—
-- src:6398 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:6399 | (b) a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:6400 | (c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity,
-- src:6401 | (ca) an e-money issuer,
-- src:6402 | (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, . . . a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6403 | (e) a person who carries on insurance market activity or
-- src:6404 | (f) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1).
@ref s 467(2) The facts about a member of a group (src:6397-6404)
DECLARE `s 467 member of a group` HAS
    `s 467 the member is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member is a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member is a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member is an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member carries on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 467 the member is a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A member is within a paragraph, or not, or not known (paragraphs (c) and (d) turn on whether the member is a small company).
-- src:6397 | (2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is—
-- src:6398 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:6399 | (b) a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:6400 | (c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity,
-- src:6401 | (ca) an e-money issuer,
-- src:6402 | (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, . . . a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6403 | (e) a person who carries on insurance market activity or
-- src:6404 | (f) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1).
@ref s 467(2) A member of the group within one of the paragraphs (src:6397-6404)
GIVEN member IS A `s 467 member of a group`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(2) the member is within one of the paragraphs` MEANS
    LET `outside (c) and (d) the answer is plain` MEANS
               member's `s 467 the member is a traded company`
            OR member's `s 467 the member is a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
            OR member's `s 467 the member is an e-money issuer`
            OR member's `s 467 the member carries on insurance market activity`
            OR member's `s 467 the member is a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme`
    IN IF `outside (c) and (d) the answer is plain`
       THEN JUST TRUE
       ELSE CONSIDER member's `s 467 the member is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2)`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                -- a small company: (d) applies, (c) ("other than a small company") does not
                IF member's `s 467 the member is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "if any of its members is" not met by this member): "A group is ineligible if any of its members is— ... (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, ... a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
                -- not a small company: (c) applies, (d) does not
                IF member's `s 467 the member is a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "if any of its members is" not met by this member): "(c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the member is a small company is not known

-- src:6397 | (2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is—
-- src:6398 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:6399 | (b) a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:6400 | (c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity,
-- src:6401 | (ca) an e-money issuer,
-- src:6402 | (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, . . . a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6403 | (e) a person who carries on insurance market activity or
-- src:6404 | (f) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1).
@ref s 467(2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is within a paragraph (src:6397-6404)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 467 member of a group`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(2) the group is ineligible` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN m YIELD `s 467(2) the member is within one of the paragraphs` m EQUALS JUST TRUE) members
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF all (GIVEN m YIELD `s 467(2) the member is within one of the paragraphs` m EQUALS JUST FALSE) members
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "A group is ineligible if any of its members is"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a member is within a paragraph is not known

-- (1): not entitled to take advantage of the medium-sized provisions if, at any time within the financial year, the company
-- was (a) a public company, (b) a company within (i) to (iii), (ba) an e-money issuer, or (c) a member of an ineligible group.
-- Titled as the bar: JUST TRUE means the company is not entitled to take advantage.
-- src:6389 | (1) A company is not entitled to take advantage of any of the provisions of this Part relating to companies qualifying as medium-sized if it was at any time within the financial year in question—
-- src:6390 | (a) a public company,
-- src:6391 | (b) a company that—
-- src:6392 | (i) has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to carry on a regulated activity, or
-- src:6393 | (ii) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:6394 | (iii) is a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1), or
-- src:6395 | (ba) an e-money issuer, or
-- src:6396 | (c) a member of an ineligible group.
@ref s 467(1) A company is not entitled to take advantage of the medium-sized provisions (src:6389-6396)
GIVEN `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a company that has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a company that carries on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year in question an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 467(2) the group of which the company was at any time within the financial year in question a member is ineligible` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(1) the section bars the company from taking advantage of the medium-sized provisions` MEANS
    IF    `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a public company`
       OR `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a company that has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity`
       OR `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a company that carries on insurance market activity`
       OR `the company was at any time within the financial year in question a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021`
       OR `the company was at any time within the financial year in question an e-money issuer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 467(2) the group of which the company was at any time within the financial year in question a member is ineligible`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met in each of (a) to (c)): "A company is not entitled to take advantage of any of the provisions of this Part relating to companies qualifying as medium-sized if it was at any time within the financial year in question— (a) a public company, (b) ..., (ba) an e-money issuer, or (c) a member of an ineligible group"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is ineligible is not known

-- (4): this section does not prevent a company from taking advantage of s 417(7) by reason only of its having been a member of an ineligible group.
-- src:6406 | (4) This section does not prevent a company from taking advantage of section 417(7) (business review: non-financial information) by reason only of its having been a member of an ineligible group at any time within the financial year in question.
@ref s 467(4) The section does not prevent the company from taking advantage of section 417(7) by reason only of membership of an ineligible group (src:6406)
GIVEN `the only reason the company would be prevented is that it was a member of an ineligible group at some time within the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467(4) the section prevents the company from taking advantage of section 417(7)` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the company would be prevented is that it was a member of an ineligible group at some time within the financial year in question`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not prevent a company from taking advantage of section 417(7) (business review: non-financial information) by reason only of its having been a member of an ineligible group at any time within the financial year in question."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of "by reason only of its having been a member of an ineligible group"
